        <p><strong>The locality story:</strong> this is what natural word order buys you. Four of the five arcs connect immediate or near neighbors; the longest ("mat" back to the root "sat") spans just three positions. A comprehender — human or model — never has to hold a dependent in memory for long before its head arrives. Averaging the arc lengths gives the metric used throughout this project:</p>

        <div class="code-block-label">Average Dependency Length</div>
        <div class="code-block">ADL = (1/n) · Σ | pos(wᵢ) − pos(head(wᵢ)) |</div>

        <div class="figure-shell">
          <div class="figure-caption">Figure 2. A relative clause forces one long arc. ADL = (1+1+1+1+2+2+5)/7 = <strong>1.86</strong>.</div>
